            <div xml:id="d229">

                <pb facs="0243" n="231" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg231"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.24/536: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >White</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-09-02T12:00:00-05:00">September 2,
                        1943—noon.</date><lb/>[Received 1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>156. Reference Department’s circular telegram dated August 31, 4 p.m.<anchor
                        n="53" xml:id="d229-f1"/> Embassy with Dowling participating discussed
                    proposed simplified export control procedure with Défly, head of Country Agency,
                    who readily accepted on behalf of Government. Moreover, he expressed
                    gratification and indicated he would be prepared to institute new change with
                    minimum of delay as soon as date and procedure fixed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
